(5155104, 713647, 65405, '<td valign="top">I adore your photographs, stunning creativity.  Thank you for visiting my portfolio and the comment, much appreciated and I''ll keep visiting you and your work....very inspirational.<br/>Suzer<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-12-28 16:11:42.</i></td>', 'I adore your photographs, stunning creativity.  Thank you for visiting my portfolio and the comment, much appreciated and I''ll keep visiting you and your work....very inspirational.Suzer', '2008-12-28 16:11:02.000000', '2008-12-28 16:11:42.000000', 0),
(5165276, 713645, 30982, '<td valign="top">I have not seen this one before.  Interesting that some find it sad - I see it as very hopeful.  Perhaps that''s due in part to the fact I know it''s yours, after the fact and all, and I tend to see your work in general as positive and hopeful.  He''s out, he''s about, and he has a grand view ahead of him.  Nice choice to use B&amp;W, too.</td>', 'I have not seen this one before.  Interesting that some find it sad - I see it as very hopeful.  Perhaps that''s due in part to the fact I know it''s yours, after the fact and all, and I tend to see your work in general as positive and hopeful.  He''s out, he''s about, and he has a grand view ahead of him.  Nice choice to use B&W, too.', '2009-01-02 14:01:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5240682, 713500, 76198, '<td valign="top">It''s bizarre to me that people didn''t get this. I like it.</td>', 'It''s bizarre to me that people didn''t get this. I like it.', '2009-02-05 11:10:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5252646, 714648, 30364, '<td valign="top">I just found this!  Congratulations on your noble gesture, easily worthy of Sydney Carton.<br/> <br/>I just love looking at the votes.  57 x 1s, and 67 x 2s &amp; 3s.  Do you realize that that means nearly 60% of the voters thought ... er, thought ... well, thought nothing at all, presumably.  Can you <i>imagine</i> being like that?  What must the world look like to such people?<br/> <br/>ETA:  <i>All Our Yesterdays</i> is a beautiful title.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-02-12 06:37:26.</i></td>', 'I just found this!  Congratulations on your noble gesture, easily worthy of Sydney Carton. I just love looking at the votes.  57 x 1s, and 67 x 2s & 3s.  Do you realize that that means nearly 60% of the voters thought ... er, thought ... well, thought nothing at all, presumably.  Can you imagine being like that?  What must the world look like to such people? ETA:  All Our Yesterdays is a beautiful title.', '2009-02-12 06:31:36.000000', '2009-02-12 06:37:26.000000', 0),
